codex
I’ve found a likely rejection-level concurrency flaw: while one channel operation awaits socket readiness, actor reentrancy allows another operation to enter the same bridge. Two bridge services can snapshot and write the same outbound bytes, and channel cancellation can free a libssh2 channel pointer that a suspended read/write still holds. The current tests cover the bridge only sequentially and do not exercise live concurrent channel/cancel behavior. I’m continuing through timeout/error/metrics behavior and the reproducible build gates before fixing the verdict.
